<header>
  <h1>Pricing, Engagements & SLAs</h1>
  <p class="meta">Author: Rosario Roussin · Last updated: 2025-09-28</p>
</header>
<section class="toc">
  <h2>On this page</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#rates">What you get from hourly consulting</a></li>    <li><a href="#readiness-assessment">What’s in a cloud readiness assessment</a></li>    <li><a href="#managed-plan">Managed plan coverage</a></li>  </ul>
</section>
<section id="rates">
  <h2>What you get from hourly consulting</h2>
  <p class="answer">Hourly work covers discovery, architecture, hands‑on setup, and documentation. Expect clear estimates up front, weekly summaries, and actionable next steps. The goal is a durable hand‑off—not dependency.</p>
  <h3>Steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Discovery → plan → build → document.</li>
    <li>Set weekly goals and share progress.</li>
    <li>Deliver runbooks and credentials on hand‑off.</li>
    <li>Offer optional check‑ins after launch.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
<section id="readiness-assessment">
  <h2>What’s in a cloud readiness assessment</h2>
  <p class="answer">A short engagement that inventories systems, gaps, risks, and costs with a proposed roadmap. You’ll get a prioritized plan with budget ranges and timelines so you can decide what to do now vs later.</p>
  <h3>Steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Kickoff and scope confirmation.</li>
    <li>Inventory apps, data, and access.</li>
    <li>Risk/cost analysis; architecture sketch.</li>
    <li>Roadmap with phases, hours, and budget bands.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
<section id="managed-plan">
  <h2>Managed plan coverage</h2>
  <p class="answer">Ongoing patching, monitoring, backups, and incident response with clear SLAs. We agree on change windows and monthly reports. You keep control; we keep things healthy.</p>
  <h3>Steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Define scope and SLAs by service.</li>
    <li>Set change windows and contacts.</li>
    <li>Deliver monthly health and cost reports.</li>
    <li>Quarterly roadmap and optimization review.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
